course: dictionary
lesson: 964
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Bludger» is one of them. In Australia and New Zealand it is slang for a lazy person who lets others do the work. In the Harry Potter books it is a heavy ball in the game of Quidditch. To work out which meaning is meant, read the words around it, because they give you the clues.
explain: Read this: «In Australia a bludger is someone who lets others do the work.» The clue is "lets others do the work", so here a bludger is a lazy person. The verb "bludge" means to slack off, and "a bludge" is an easy task.
explain: Slang can be mildly insulting, so it is wise to think before you use it. When you meet a word you already know, check that its meaning still fits the sentence. If it does not, look for another meaning.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant.
fact: «Bludger» (Australia, New Zealand, slang) means a lazy person who avoids work or lets others do it.
fact: «Bludger» in Harry Potter means a heavy ball in Quidditch that flies around knocking players off their brooms.
fact: «Bludge» is a verb meaning to slack off, and «a bludge» is an easy task.
fact: «Dole bludger» is a rude name for someone who lives on unemployment money, so it is a mildly insulting slang phrase.
exercise: «In Australia a bludger is someone who lets others do the work.» What does bludger mean here? | A kind teacher who helps everyone | *A lazy person who lets others do the work | A heavy ball that knocks players off brooms | A fast runner in a race
exercise: In the Harry Potter books, what is a Bludger? | A broom that flies very fast | A player who catches the Golden Snitch | A type of old castle | *A heavy ball in Quidditch that knocks players off their brooms
exercise: Bludge is a verb. What does it mean? | To climb a tree | To sing loudly | *To slack off | To wash the car
test: In a game of Quidditch, what is the Bludger? | A kind referee who blows the whistle | *A heavy ball that knocks players off their brooms | A team captain who shouts orders | A small golden ball with wings
test: Which meaning of bludger is slang used in Australia and New Zealand? | A type of broom | A famous wizard school | A heavy ball in a sports game | *A lazy person who lets others do the work
exam: The word bludger has two meanings. What is the best way to tell which one is meant? | Skip the word and never come back to it | *Read the words around it to find the clues | Ignore the sentence and look only at the title | Guess the first meaning that comes to mind
